## TIẾNG ANH · 16:30–17:00 — Thứ Tư: Quyết định thiết kế

> *"I keep email off the request path on purpose. The handler writes a row and enqueues a job; the worker talks to Resend. If Resend is down, the user still gets a fast 200, and the job retries with backoff. The hard rule is the same as push receipts: don't retry permanent failures — a bad address stays bad. And I never log the reset token. If that shows up in Better Stack I've already lost."*

**5 từ mới:** `off the request path` · `enqueue` · `suppressed` · `deliverability` · `permanent failure`

